markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Section 6: Reasoning and Its Limits</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 9-12</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach four curriculum lessons. They trace one arc: reading logic, building logic, then questioning logic. Students debug existing code, compress a lighter lesson on autocomplete, build decision trees into working conditionals, and finally confront where rule-based AI itself breaks down, setting up why machine learning exists in Unit 2.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 9:</b> Debugging Intelligent Systems</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_9_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 9</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 10:</b> Systems Autocomplete</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_10_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 10</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 11:</b> Decision Trees</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_11_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 11</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 12:</b> Limits of Logic-Based AI</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_12_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 12</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Reframe debugging as reading and interpreting what a program actually did, not just hunting for a red error message</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get ahead of a real misconception: a program can run perfectly fine and still be wrong, with no error at all</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Walk through autocomplete in one compressed pass, this lesson now runs in a single day</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Build and traverse a decision tree, then translate its branches into working conditional code</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; Confront where rule-based AI breaks down, the moment that sets up why machine learning exists at all</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> this is the first section where the unit starts pointing beyond itself. Limits of Logic-Based AI isn't just a topic, it's the hinge the whole year turns on.</div>
</div>

<hr>

